Falsifies `system_tests::user::terminal_display_swap_tests::a_supervised_display_terminal_refuses_a_quiesce_from_anyone_but_its_supervisor`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch keeps `display_terminal` refusing everything but a quiesce on the supervisor's badge, and
drops the other half of the rule: a quiesce on any other capability is served again. A supervised
`display_terminal` then honors an application's quiesce, answers `QUIESCED`, and stops drawing
until a `CTL_RESUME` its supervisor never sends.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!` "an unbadged holder quiesced a supervised display_terminal (reply
0x51554954)", with `left: 1364543828` (`proto::QUIESCED`). Replayed red at exactly that assertion
on aarch64 on 2026-10-24 (UTC) by maintainer/terminal-quiesce-from-supervisor-only, after the test
was made to check each answer before its next call; checked together, the second call parked on
the quiesced terminal and the run ended at the watchdog instead. Re-cut the same day after a merge of main moved its
context, and replayed red at the same assertion.

diff --git a/components/src/display_terminal.rs b/components/src/display_terminal.rs
index a4d630974..6e49800dc 100644
--- a/components/src/display_terminal.rs
+++ b/components/src/display_terminal.rs
@@ -565,7 +565,7 @@ pub extern "C" fn _start(mode: u64, control: u64, start: u64) -> ! {
         // terminal until a supervisor that never asked said `CTL_RESUME`. Other badges are
         // served as unbadged.
         let from_supervisor = req.badge == proto::SUPERVISOR_BADGE;
-        if from_supervisor != (proto::operation(w0) == proto::OPERATION_QUIESCE) {
+        if from_supervisor && proto::operation(w0) != proto::OPERATION_QUIESCE {
             if let Some(to) = reply_slot {
                 reply(to, proto::BAD_REQUEST, 0);
             }
